00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.100
Well that's great dad, but, just how far is that?

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.020
Using some pixel measurements of this shot in the opening,

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:26.340
and using the average height of a lion of 3.9 feet,

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.380
I worked out that Pride Rock, at the very top, is about sixty feet tall.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.880
From a sixty foot height,

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.180
the horizon appears at 9.9 miles away.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:39.800
Meaning that Mufasa's kingdom is roughly a hundred square mile area.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:45.680
Which, unbelievably is actually the area that one would expect a pride of lions to control,

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.340
according to National Geographic.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:50.920
I don't know if the Disney animators did this much research, or just looked into it.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:55.740
But that has got to be one of the most incredible factoids I have ever uncovered by doing these episodes.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:01.780
Suffice it to say, we know that Scar brings ecological ruin to about a hundred square miles of plain lands.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.300
But then, how much deaths would that really cause?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.456
Lets start with wildebeests, one of the key herds we see in the movie.

00:15:07.456 --> 00:15:09.440
Mainly, when they're stampeding over Mufasa.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:12.440
Which has got to be one of the biggest wildebeest herds in history, by the way.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:15.240
Roughly one thousand, if you actually count them.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:18.880
That's almost twice the size of a normal herd of wildebeest.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.425
Meaning that when Scar starts out his reign,

00:15:21.425 --> 00:15:25.820
Pride Rock has one of the most vibrant, enormous wildebeest herds in Africa.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:31.400
And to chase them out of the area is gonna mean a lot of increased hunting and lost food for everyone in the Pride Land.

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:36.420
Scar wants to allow not just some hyenas, but a whole society of hyenas into the Pride Lands.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:40.980
I counted a hundred and thirty-nine total in this shot from "Be Prepared".

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.780
Which is a massive amount of hyenas to drop into one contained area.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:47.760
Usually, hyena pack sizes top out at about eighty.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.760
And with spotted hyenas, like the ones that we see in "The Lion King",

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.100
That number is usually even smaller.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.720
So how much food would a hundred and thirty-nine hyenas eat?

00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:00.640
Hyenas consume roughly eleven kilograms, or twenty-four pounds of food every week.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.220
In nature, that may include it's share of tasty wildebeest,

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:06.860
but they can also chow down on all kinds of smaller critters and even some bugs.

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:10.600
Of course, with Scar's regime giving the hyenas anything they want,

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:15.380
we can imagine a lot more of their diet is gonna be shifted towards the bigger game.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:19.000
Using the slaughter weight, or eatable weight of a wildebeest,

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.220
we can calculate that eighty to a hundred kilograms of wildebeest

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:25.780
is gonna be enough to feed about seven to nine hyenas for a week.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:32.000
That means that each. Week. This massive hyena pack is gonna be chewing through about twenty wildebeest.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.880
Now of course, we also have the lions.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:38.160
And lions don't just eat wildebeests, but we can use research documents

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:43.100
like the "Seasonal Diet and Prey Preference of the African Lion in a Waterhole-Driven Semi-Arid Savanna"

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:49.520
to figure out just how many other animals the lions would need to be killing in their normal distribution to feed just the hyenas.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:52.680
So each year, the combination of the hyenas and the lions would have to kill

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.180
a hundred and ten buffalo,

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.320
twenty seven elephants,

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.340
forty giraffes,

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.360
fifty-three kudus,

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.340
thirty zebras,

00:16:58.340 --> 00:16:59.540
forty-four wildebeests,

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:00.760
twenty warthogs,

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.100
and seven impalas.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:05.440
So, that's a lot of animal death, but how long does this go on for?

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:10.520
Well, when Mufasa dies, Simba's height indicates he's between two and four months old.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:15.960
And when he returns to Pride Rock, he's a fully maned adult, which puts him at about five years old.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:18.520
So assuming five years of Scar's rule,

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:21.800
and multiplying that by our three hundred and thirty-one kills per year,

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:25.820
brings us to one-thousand six-hundred and fifty-five extra deaths,

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:32.080
due directly to Scar's promise to share his food with this enormous one hundred and thirty-nine hyena pack.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:37.460
"Stick with me, and you'll never go hungry again!"

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:38.960
Oh yeah, and then Scar dies in the end.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:42.300
And that, my friends, is what it looks like to get into the big leagues.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:48.140
The new number to beat is "Lion King" with one-thousand, six-hundred and sixty deaths.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:54.320
After fifty-three movies with a whopping total of three-thousand, five-hundred and eighteen total deaths,

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:58.860
we only have five contenders remaining in our little battle royale.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:07.460
Will "Mulan", "Dinosaur", "Atlantis", "Hercules", or "Moana" be able to take the crown from the king, "The Lion King"?

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:13.440
We're now up to entire armies dying, extinction-level events, and acts of god, or rather gods.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:17.660
Of the remaining contestants, let me know who you think has the edge in the comments,

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:18.880
and then get out your umbrellas,

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:22.380
because it's gonna be raining G-rated corpses on the next episode.

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:24.500
Who will win this literal death battle?

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.140
I am dying to find out.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:30.440
But remember.. It's all just a theory.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.460
A Film Theory!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.420
Aaaaaand..... cut!

